  "name": "Diatom Assemblages from the Pliocene-Pleistocene Boundary Beds in Kamchatka, Russia",
  "description": "The identification of North Pacific diatom assemblages in the Olkhovian Formation of eastern Kamchatka and their correlation with the paleomagnetic time scale allows accurate placement of the Pliocene-Pleistocene boundary in the Kamchatka region. Analysis of the composition of the diatom flora makes possible a paleogeographic reconstruction of the shelf region in the western Bering Sea during the latest Pliocene and early Pleistocene.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To show the diatom assemblages from the Pliocene-Pleistocene boundary beds in Kamchatka, Russia",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23563850",
